; MifFOTBuilder — the `-t mif` backend: Kathleen Marszalek's and Paul
; Prescod's FrameMaker Interchange Format writer. Ported from
; ~/repos/dazzle/jade/MifFOTBuilder.cxx (C++ oracle, openjade 1.3.3-pre1;
; JADE_MIF defined, NDEBUG undefined — the reference asserts are live and
; port as loud exit-17 traps). The C# mirror has no MIF backend; the C++ is
; the only source.
;
; Output model: a MIF DOCUMENT OBJECT MODEL, not a stream. The builder grows
; one `MifBookComponent` per simple-page-sequence (plus the implicit first
; one) holding the catalogs (Pgf/Color/Ruling/Tbl), the anchored frames, the
; tables, the master/body pages with their text rects, and the text flows;
; flow-object content is written into per-tag-stream byte buffers (the
; reference MifTmpOutputByteStream) that are spliced into the file at commit
; time. `commit()` writes one file per book component (a `<Book 5.0>` root
; plus `1.mif`, `2.mif`, … when there is more than one) — the reference
; MifDoc destructor.
;
; Paragraph and font formats are DELTA formats: every `Pgf`/`Font` statement
; prints only the properties that differ from the enclosing state
; (`compare`/`setFrom`/`updateFrom` + a per-property set-bit mask), which is
; why the format records carry their `*_set` masks everywhere.
;
; Cross-references, hypertext links and index entries are resolved in a
; SECOND PASS: `<Marker>`/`<XRef>` cannot be emitted until it is known
; whether anything referenced the element, so the content stream carries a
; one-byte escape (NUL) plus a 4-byte index into `cross_ref_infos`, and the
; commit-time splice expands it.
;
; Reference quirks reproduced deliberately (verified against the reference
; binary): the `case SP_LETTER2('D','E')` arm of computePgfLanguage has NO
; `break`, so language "DE" falls through and yields `French`; the
; T_dimension format loses the sign of values in (-1000, 0); the
; `fXRefSrcText` enumerator has no initialiser and is therefore 5, not 8;
; `startLineField`'s `PgfNumTabs + leadingTab ? 2 : 1` parses as
; `(PgfNumTabs + leadingTab) ? 2 : 1`; and `TablePart::begin` wipes the
; column list a table declared before its first table-part, which is what
; makes the `missing table column flow object` warning fire on ordinary
; documents.
;
; RBMM: everything lives on the builder's page (the run arena) — the whole
; document model has to survive until commit anyway, so nothing is ever
; freed; the reference's `delete`s are simply dropped. The stacks are
; slot-reused pointer arrays with depth cursors.

